<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Tremor history and examination with the MDS 1608 classification (rest, postural, and kinetic tremor; distribution; parkinsonism, dystonia, ataxia); TSH, metabolic panel, liver tests, and blood count; a medication, caffeine, and alcohol review. Guideline: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011; reaffirmed 2025) (2011); Consensus Statement on the classification of tremors, from the task force on tremor of the International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society (2018); MDS evidence-based review of treatments for essential tremor (2019) [S]</item><item>Movement disorders neurology consultation to confirm the tremor type, exclude early Parkinson disease, and advise on treatment. Guideline: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011; reaffirmed 2025) (2011); Consensus Statement on the classification of tremors, from the task force on tremor of the International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society (2018); MDS evidence-based review of treatments for essential tremor (2019) [S]</item><item>Alcohol: AUDIT screening and a brief intervention (feedback, advice, and a goal of no more than 14 drinks a week and 4 on any day); follow-up of drinking at each visit and GGT after eight to ten weeks. Guideline: Unhealthy Alcohol Use in Adolescents and Adults: Screening and Behavioral Counseling Interventions (2018); Helping Patients Who Drink Too Much: A Clinician&apos;s Guide (2005) [S]</item><item>Handwriting sample and Archimedes spiral at each visit; cut coffee to two cups a day, none after midday. Guideline: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011; reaffirmed 2025) (2011); Consensus Statement on the classification of tremors, from the task force on tremor of the International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society (2018); MDS evidence-based review of treatments for essential tremor (2019) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
